<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Some things are faster said than typed. The microphone button sits in the toolbar beside the message input, next to the attachment and formatting buttons. It records up to a minute of audio and sends it as a separate message."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_microphone}>{dgettext("help_features", "Recording One")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Press the microphone and allow access when the browser asks. While you speak, the recording replaces the input: a red dot, a clock that counts up, a button to discard it and a button to send it."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The send button ends the recording and sends it. The discard button deletes it. In both cases the microphone turns off."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_send}>
  {dgettext("help_features", "Only the Recording Is Sent")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Only the recording is sent. Text you typed stays in the input. Files waiting to be attached stay too."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_warning}>
  {dgettext("help_features", "A Minute, and Then It Stops")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A recording stops by itself after one minute and is sent as it is. After a minute it stops being something the other person can take in during a conversation, which is what writing is for."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_display}>{dgettext("help_features", "Where It Is Offered")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "On a desktop and on a phone, in any browser that can record. If the browser cannot record, the microphone does not appear, and the attachment button can still send an audio file."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-message-attachments">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Message Attachments")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
